      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>scale the window or drink water... it doesn't change the fact that the machine keeps turning. those small steps feel like trying to put a bandaid on a broken limb. i'm just waiting for the day the machine finally breaks me, but i feel like i'm just letting it happen. like i'm just a ghost haunting my own life. i don't see how any of those little things make the cycle any less hollow.",
